---
import ExampleSection from "../../ExampleSection.astro";
import ExampleCodeBlock from "../../ExampleCodeBlock.astro";
import CodeSnippet from "../../CodeSnippet.astro";
---

<ExampleSection id="anchored-labels" eyebrow="Foundations" title="Authored anchored labels" status="partial">
    <Fragment slot="description">
        Real labels can opt into CSS Anchor Positioning relative to their associated thumbs. The minimum uses implicit
        wrapping, while the maximum uses an explicit <code>for</code>/<code>id</code> association; both labels retain normal
        activation behavior.
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="disclosure">
        <code>RangeGroupAnchoredLabels</code> depends on <code>RangeGroup</code>, is independent of
        <code>SliderPseudoElements</code>, and has no script-visible detection surface. Chromium supplies only each
        label&rsquo;s implicit relationship to its thumb. The absolute positioning and <code>position-area</code> below are
        entirely author CSS; there is no automatic UA label layout. Without native <code>&lt;rangegroup&gt;</code>, the
        labels and fallback sliders return to normal flow.
    </Fragment>
    <div slot="demo">
        <style is:global>
            #anchored-label-range {
                position: relative;
                margin-block: 1rem 2.5rem;
            }
            html[data-rangegroup-anchored-labels="on"] #anchored-label-range > .anchored-thumb-label {
                position: absolute;
                position-anchor: auto;
                position-area: block-end;
                margin-block-start: 0.45rem;
                padding: 0.2rem 0.45rem;
                border: 1px solid var(--border);
                border-radius: 5px;
                background: var(--surface);
                color: var(--text-strong);
                font-size: 0.75rem;
                font-weight: 650;
                white-space: nowrap;
                cursor: pointer;
            }
            .prototype-fallback #anchored-label-range > .anchored-thumb-label {
                position: static;
                display: grid;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                color: var(--text-muted);
                font-size: 0.85rem;
                font-weight: 600;
            }
            .prototype-fallback #anchored-label-range > .anchored-thumb-label input,
            .prototype-fallback #anchored-label-range > input[type="range"] {
                width: 100%;
            }
        </style>
        <rangegroup id="anchored-label-range" min="0" max="100">
            <legend class="visually-hidden">Delivery window</legend>
            <label class="anchored-thumb-label">
                Earliest
                <input type="range" name="delivery-start" min="0" max="100" value="25" />
            </label>
            <label class="anchored-thumb-label" for="delivery-end">Latest</label>
            <input id="delivery-end" type="range" name="delivery-end" min="0" max="100" value="75" />
        </rangegroup>
    </div>
    <ExampleCodeBlock slot="code">
        <CodeSnippet
            lang="html"
            code={`
<rangegroup id="delivery-window" min="0" max="100">
  <legend>Delivery window</legend>

  <!-- Implicit association by wrapping. -->
  <label class="thumb-label">
    Earliest
    <input type="range" name="delivery-start"
           min="0" max="100" value="25">
  </label>

  <!-- Explicit association remains activatable. -->
  <label class="thumb-label" for="delivery-end">Latest</label>
  <input id="delivery-end" type="range" name="delivery-end"
         min="0" max="100" value="75">
</rangegroup>
`}
        />
        <CodeSnippet
            lang="css"
            code={`
#delivery-window {
  position: relative;
}

/* Chromium supplies the implicit thumb relationship only.
   Authors opt into all visible placement. */
#delivery-window > .thumb-label {
  position: absolute;
  position-anchor: auto;
  position-area: block-end;
  margin-block-start: .45rem;
}

/* A non-supporting browser keeps the real labels and inputs usable.
   The showcase applies this override from its detected fallback state. */
.prototype-fallback #delivery-window > .thumb-label {
  position: static;
}
`}
        />
    </ExampleCodeBlock>
</ExampleSection>
